In render/json.go, JSON.Render does not return the error — it panics with it:

    func (r JSON) Render(w http.ResponseWriter) (err error) {
        if err = WriteJSON(w, r.Data); err != nil {
            panic(err)
        }
        return
    }

So a non-nil error from WriteJSON results in panic(err) (the named return `err` is set but the function panics before returning). Note this is the only renderer in that file that panics; IndentedJSON, SecureJSON, JsonpJSON, AsciiJSON and PureJSON all return the error instead. WriteJSON itself is `func WriteJSON(w http.ResponseWriter, obj any) error` and returns the json.Marshal error or the w.Write error.
